WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.608 --> 01:09.235
I want you to listen to me.
I'm gonna say this again.

01:10.028 --> 01:15.784
I did not have sexual relations
with that woman, Miss Lewinsky.

01:16.534 --> 01:17.494
I never told anybody…

01:17.577 --> 01:19.204
The strongest wind

01:20.205 --> 01:22.665
is the one that blows within one's heart.

01:23.833 --> 01:26.586
No power on earth can overcome it.

01:26.669 --> 01:29.422
I'm completely innocent
in all this.

01:29.506 --> 01:31.716
Absolutely guilt-free.

01:33.259 --> 01:35.553
No guilt whatsoever.

01:36.513 --> 01:37.472
So then, why?

01:38.848 --> 01:43.144
Why am I no longer the chief
and just put out to pasture?

01:46.940 --> 01:48.191
Hey, Park Yeong-ran.

01:49.234 --> 01:50.401
Come here.

01:57.492 --> 02:00.370
You disrespect me too, huh?

02:01.079 --> 02:04.666
I said to come over here.
What the hell do you do at home, huh?

02:05.291 --> 02:07.544
You get to eat white rice
with the money I make for you,

02:07.627 --> 02:09.712
and you can't even watch our kid?!

02:09.796 --> 02:11.714
She behaves like that
because she takes after you.

02:11.798 --> 02:13.133
I know everything!

02:13.758 --> 02:15.426
Go to sleep if you're drunk!

02:15.927 --> 02:19.764
What, little jerk? Whose kid are you?
Whose side are you on?

02:19.848 --> 02:22.183
Father, do you even know how old I am?

02:23.935 --> 02:25.812
Ha!

02:29.482 --> 02:31.276
Oh! Hey.

02:31.359 --> 02:32.777
Hey. Hey, you punk!

02:32.861 --> 02:34.654
Maybe you never came to see me
on sports day

02:34.737 --> 02:36.239
because I'm not your kid, after all.

02:36.823 --> 02:39.784
While you hauled ass to see spring flowers
or mountains in the winter…

02:39.868 --> 02:41.369
"Hauled ass," really?

02:41.452 --> 02:43.580
…Mom hasn't ever missed a day
fixing us a hot lunch.

02:43.663 --> 02:44.998
Hey!

02:45.748 --> 02:48.877
And who brought you
your stepmom here, huh?

02:49.794 --> 02:51.880
I can always get you a new stepmom,

02:51.963 --> 02:54.340
but I'm your genitor!

02:54.424 --> 02:56.843
If you guys are gonna break up,
I'm going with her.

02:56.926 --> 02:57.760
What boy?

02:57.844 --> 02:59.679
I'm treating you like a dad

03:00.889 --> 03:02.682
only because she lives with you, you know.

03:05.018 --> 03:06.144
Bring the broom here.

03:07.896 --> 03:09.230
Where's the broom?

03:09.898 --> 03:12.734
-Huh? Where's the… Where's the…
-Oh-seong, go to your room.

03:12.817 --> 03:13.818
Ow!

03:13.902 --> 03:15.403
You shouldn't be like that to your dad.

03:15.486 --> 03:18.448
Split up with him already!
Come on! What's there to lose?

03:18.531 --> 03:20.241
-But I…
-Who put this here?

03:20.325 --> 03:21.659
I am staying with your father.

03:21.743 --> 03:23.953
-Who put this year? Oh, ow.
-I'm staying with him.

03:28.625 --> 03:30.585
My God! Jeez!

03:38.092 --> 03:39.469
I knew it.

03:40.220 --> 03:42.305
You'd never survive without me.

03:43.556 --> 03:47.101
You get to put food on the table
thanks to the money I earn.

03:47.810 --> 03:48.645
Huh?

03:49.729 --> 03:51.648
The food I bring to our house.

03:52.899 --> 03:54.025
I'll stay.

03:57.946 --> 03:59.072
I will stay.

03:59.155 --> 04:00.740
How dare…

04:01.699 --> 04:03.368
We'll grow old together.

04:04.994 --> 04:08.456
Then, I'll see you in paradise.

04:16.464 --> 04:19.175
KNOCK
YOU BETTER KNOCK

04:31.354 --> 04:33.106
Oh shit.

04:45.535 --> 04:46.369
Get out.

04:47.787 --> 04:50.331
You little…

04:52.709 --> 04:55.086
God, I wish I could knock you out
with a damn flying kick now.

04:55.169 --> 04:56.671
I said, get out!

04:56.754 --> 04:57.588
Good God.

04:58.214 --> 04:59.382
God, God, God.

05:03.011 --> 05:04.053
Mom!

05:04.137 --> 05:07.348
Listen, if you were Han-eum,
I would've given you a beating.

05:07.432 --> 05:08.599
You know that?

05:08.683 --> 05:11.311
You have a boyfriend, and you look like
you're a battle-worn soldier?

05:12.061 --> 05:14.397
Why… why do you have a photo
of Hwang Shin-hye?

05:14.480 --> 05:16.649
If you wanna look like her,
you'll need a different body.

05:16.733 --> 05:18.568
Why can't you just leave me alone?

05:18.651 --> 05:21.195
Of all people,
how could you be involved with their son?

05:21.279 --> 05:24.365
You idiot. His mother and our, our…

05:25.491 --> 05:27.910
-Damn it.
-What about her?

05:27.994 --> 05:29.871
Don't worry about it.

05:30.913 --> 05:32.749
You're gonna be embarrassed
when you find out.

05:32.832 --> 05:35.376
Stop this bullshit
while I'm still being nice.

05:37.920 --> 05:39.297
Let me think about it, then.

05:43.509 --> 05:45.094
You go and tell the guy…

05:48.389 --> 05:50.266
that I'll kill him
if I ever see him again.

05:57.148 --> 05:59.275
Let's just end it, okay?

05:59.359 --> 06:02.320
No, I don't want to!

06:02.403 --> 06:04.655
Is this because of those bastards
Oh-seong and Han-eum?

06:04.739 --> 06:06.366
Or is it because of my father?

06:06.866 --> 06:12.288
I am me, and my father is my father.
And I don't listen to my dad anyway.

06:12.372 --> 06:15.708
Look, don't tell anyone
that we're together anymore.

06:16.334 --> 06:19.212
Don't cut in line at the store
and expect me to serve you.

06:20.755 --> 06:23.257
If you're going to the roller rink,
please go to Ssangbong.

06:23.341 --> 06:25.385
No, I'm gonna be your girlfriend.

06:25.468 --> 06:28.137
I won't let you date
anyone else but me. No way.

06:28.805 --> 06:30.681
If you do, I'm gonna beat up those girls.

06:30.765 --> 06:33.935
You don't believe I will?
You don't believe I will?!

06:34.977 --> 06:36.270
Oh, I think you will.

06:36.354 --> 06:38.439
I won't let you end us.

06:38.523 --> 06:41.025
I can't.

06:41.734 --> 06:44.195
-One more thing, Bu Hyeon-suk.
-What?

06:51.369 --> 06:52.412
You be well.

06:59.794 --> 07:00.837
They're crying.

07:04.298 --> 07:05.675
You son of a bitch!

07:07.009 --> 07:10.721
Don't ever let me see you again.

07:10.805 --> 07:12.265
I'll kill you dead!

07:14.142 --> 07:16.769
You're breaking up
because you got your ass kicked?

07:16.853 --> 07:19.272
Great! So I'll tell my brothers
to keep doing it!

07:19.355 --> 07:20.898
To beat you up each time they see you!

07:20.982 --> 07:22.900
They ever beat you, huh?

07:25.319 --> 07:26.988
Okay, fine. Let's run away.

07:27.572 --> 07:29.198
Make sure they don't catch us.

07:29.282 --> 07:32.869
The arcade, the rolling skating rink,
Chilseongtong. I can't go anywhere.

07:33.619 --> 07:36.539
Your brothers' friends
are just everywhere.

07:36.622 --> 07:38.708
I got on the bus yesterday,

07:38.791 --> 07:41.169
and the bus driver
was one of their friends.

07:42.545 --> 07:45.840
He told me to stay on
until the end of the line.

07:48.134 --> 07:50.136
How can I live here now, huh?

07:50.219 --> 07:52.221
I need to live too.

07:53.639 --> 07:54.557
Then we'll run.

07:55.266 --> 07:56.517
Let's run away.

07:57.435 --> 08:00.021
-What?
-I can't live like this either.

08:00.104 --> 08:03.065
My father even broke off my bedroom door.

08:05.026 --> 08:06.360
Do you wanna run away together?

08:06.444 --> 08:08.738
You know, he even said
that if I keep seeing you,

08:08.821 --> 08:11.616
he would shave my head
and send me to a monastery.

08:11.699 --> 08:13.326
You believe he'll do it?

08:13.409 --> 08:16.078
So then, all of your friends
would be monks and nuns.

08:17.872 --> 08:19.081
Are we gonna run or not?

08:23.169 --> 08:25.379
Answer me. Are you or not?

08:26.506 --> 08:28.466
I don't know.

08:38.100 --> 08:41.604
Honk. Honk. Keep honking.
Keep honking the horn.

08:42.188 --> 08:43.648
Keep honking.

08:45.650 --> 08:48.027
They look like
the center of the Korean flag.

08:48.110 --> 08:51.822
They're having
the time of their lives there.

08:51.906 --> 08:53.908
This is their springtime right now.

08:53.991 --> 08:57.787
I mean, is it springtime that's
the problem, or is it their bloodline?

08:57.870 --> 09:00.540
-I love you.
-I love you too.

09:00.623 --> 09:04.502
In retrospect,
one realizes springtime was a celebration.

09:05.836 --> 09:07.380
Come in, son.

09:07.463 --> 09:09.840
But to new growing buds,
spring feels like war.

09:09.924 --> 09:10.758
Hello.

09:12.760 --> 09:13.928
You come to my son's too?

09:14.512 --> 09:17.431
Like when new buds push their heads
through the concrete.

09:28.609 --> 09:30.528
You don't even know how to ladle soup.

09:33.239 --> 09:37.660
-Did your mother not teach you?
-Ah, it's, uh, the seaweed is all tangled.

09:38.244 --> 09:39.537
Hey, keep your hands out!

09:40.371 --> 09:41.872
We don't do that in our home.

09:49.547 --> 09:51.007
The two of you are here. Oh.

09:51.591 --> 09:53.134
This is a great birthday.

10:15.865 --> 10:18.409
This kimchi is… is so, so good.

10:19.493 --> 10:21.579
It's hard to find good kimchi in Seoul.

10:21.662 --> 10:24.248
I mean, uh,
I don't mean kimchi in Seoul is all bad--

10:24.332 --> 10:25.416
I bought it.

10:26.667 --> 10:28.127
Mm. Mm.

10:30.046 --> 10:31.964
It's been a while
since I've had homemade food.

10:32.882 --> 10:34.342
It feels like I could eat two bowls.

10:34.425 --> 10:36.510
We value portion control.

10:40.306 --> 10:43.684
Do your parents know…
you come to a boy's apartment?

10:45.102 --> 10:48.439
She's not here a lot.
I invited her since it's my birthday.

10:49.774 --> 10:51.359
That wasn't a question for you.

10:55.363 --> 10:56.572
So, Geum-myeong.

10:57.573 --> 11:00.284
This isn't Yeong-beom's apartment.
This is my place.

11:01.160 --> 11:02.453
I got this for him.

11:03.454 --> 11:07.166
I don't… want you
frequenting my apartment.

11:08.042 --> 11:11.879
-Mother.
-I don't want Geum-myeong in my apartment.

11:14.590 --> 11:17.927
Of course, continue dating.
Learn how romance works.

11:18.636 --> 11:21.931
Mom, I told you. I'm dating Geum-myeong
'cause I plan on marrying her.

11:25.017 --> 11:27.561
You asked for a place near school,
and this is so…

11:30.981 --> 11:32.525
so…

11:35.027 --> 11:36.570
You are my pride.

11:36.654 --> 11:38.572
And now my pride is damaged.

11:41.200 --> 11:44.704
Love in our hearts
was a wind that made each of us waver.

11:44.787 --> 11:46.997
And that wind felt like a typhoon.

11:47.081 --> 11:50.668
Is your family a conglomerate?
Like Samsung or Hyundai?

11:50.751 --> 11:53.212
Is your family really
so much wealthier than mine?

11:56.173 --> 11:58.175
We go to the same school.
My parents care about me

11:58.259 --> 11:59.552
as much as yours care about you.

11:59.635 --> 12:02.096
Why should I feel ashamed
that I can't ladle soup, huh?

12:02.179 --> 12:04.557
Do you ladle well?
Did your mother teach you?

12:04.640 --> 12:06.809
I'm terrible at that.

12:07.476 --> 12:09.812
It's so unfair.

12:11.021 --> 12:13.524
Everything just feels so wrong.

12:13.607 --> 12:16.819
I… I just… I just feel like a cheap clown,

12:16.902 --> 12:19.697
dancing for a lady who won't like me,
no matter what I'm doing.

12:19.780 --> 12:22.950
I can't stand being treated like this.
You get that?

12:23.033 --> 12:24.702
I despise that feeling.

12:32.710 --> 12:33.878
DIGESTIVE DRINK

12:38.340 --> 12:39.925
Why did you have so much food?

12:40.843 --> 12:43.387
I wanted to try and impress your mother.

12:43.471 --> 12:45.222
That's why I ate so much.

12:46.140 --> 12:49.101
What girl does not want to impress
her boyfriend's mother?

12:49.685 --> 12:52.730
I won't get engaged to Mom's pride.
Do you understand me?

12:57.610 --> 12:58.778
Now you have to decide.

12:58.861 --> 13:02.323
Choose if you wanna be
a good husband or a good son.

13:02.406 --> 13:03.407
You can only be one.

13:04.033 --> 13:07.453
Please, I really don't want a man
who needs to please everyone.

13:07.536 --> 13:11.332
Before you think about proposing,
you must choose one or the other.

13:11.415 --> 13:14.960
Well, who… who could pick one
over the other though? I…

13:15.586 --> 13:17.588
-No man would ever…
-Some men would.

13:18.255 --> 13:19.089
What?

13:19.632 --> 13:21.133
My father did it.

13:21.926 --> 13:22.760
Oh.

13:24.428 --> 13:26.347
Let me make myself clear in this.

13:27.181 --> 13:29.809
I won't marry your mother's son, okay?

13:31.811 --> 13:33.896
I don't know why
she was emotional

13:33.979 --> 13:35.189
about everything at the time.

13:35.272 --> 13:37.525
She was like an owl
that screeched all night

13:37.608 --> 13:39.485
at the slightest sound of a breeze.

13:41.987 --> 13:44.740
This is Kim Gi-deok on Two O'Clock Date.

13:45.866 --> 13:50.579
So I believe the '90s is indeed
the renaissance of mainstream culture.

13:51.330 --> 13:54.375
You could say it's the roaring '90s.

13:54.458 --> 13:55.835
I love this painting.

13:55.918 --> 13:57.753
I guess he doesn't wanna be
Picasso anymore.

13:57.837 --> 14:00.464
See? You can do your job right.

14:00.548 --> 14:01.882
It's so clear.

14:01.966 --> 14:03.926
You can tell what this movie is about.

14:04.009 --> 14:08.055
Just looking at it makes me
wanna perform the Lambada. Yeah?

14:09.557 --> 14:10.641
Good job.

14:12.810 --> 14:15.187
Oh, that lady's back again.

14:15.271 --> 14:17.731
She always figures out
when it's opening night.

14:17.815 --> 14:20.776
Where does she get
the resale tickets?

14:20.860 --> 14:23.821
I've never sold her any tickets before.

14:24.405 --> 14:26.365
Do you think they might be counterfeit?

14:51.724 --> 14:53.142
We're not interested.

14:53.642 --> 14:55.019
Okay, listen.

14:55.102 --> 14:58.314
-We don't want resale tickets.
-No, I just have a question.

14:59.023 --> 15:01.442
Does that look like Choi Jin-sil?

15:03.861 --> 15:06.113
Maybe it doesn't look like her?

15:06.196 --> 15:10.117
-I think it looks like her.
-Oh, that means this one is well-drawn.

15:10.200 --> 15:12.286
-Sorry?
-Or not. I don't know.

15:12.953 --> 15:14.330
Oh, no. I'm sure. I'm sure, yes.

15:14.413 --> 15:18.083
I heard that was drawn by an art student.

15:18.959 --> 15:19.793
Ah.

15:20.377 --> 15:23.380
Why won't people ever look at
that piece of art before they walk in?

15:23.464 --> 15:25.424
Maybe they're busy, but it makes me sad

15:25.507 --> 15:27.843
that they won't look at
the painting even once.

15:28.469 --> 15:29.637
It really breaks my heart.

15:30.220 --> 15:33.641
A Picasso lived in
the basement floor of the Cannes Theater,

15:33.724 --> 15:36.060
and to someone,
this theater was their Louvre.

15:36.143 --> 15:38.938
Stop! Don't resell tickets!
Not in my theater!

15:39.021 --> 15:41.482
Scalping is a societal menace! You hear?

15:41.565 --> 15:43.275
No selling resale tickets!

15:43.984 --> 15:45.486
Stop it, I said!

15:46.153 --> 15:48.364
Does that man really think I'm a scalper?

16:05.464 --> 16:08.759
Since you're already here,
you may as well watch a movie.

16:10.177 --> 16:12.638
This one coming out in two days
is really good, I hear.

16:12.721 --> 16:15.182
We're showing it again
because it was so popular.

16:16.308 --> 16:19.436
Oh, no. You really shouldn't
give out free tickets.

16:19.520 --> 16:22.064
Ah, sure, but you're not just anyone.

16:22.648 --> 16:26.151
This is an employee benefit
offered by the owner himself.

16:28.320 --> 16:30.656
Come at 2:00 p.m. on Monday.
It's normally empty then,

16:30.739 --> 16:32.950
so it'll feel like
you rented the theater for yourself.

16:33.033 --> 16:33.909
Thank you.

16:34.451 --> 16:36.370
By the way,
could you please not tell my son

16:36.453 --> 16:38.455
that I come here to look at his paintings?

16:39.456 --> 16:41.375
Chung-seob doesn't know I come here.

16:41.458 --> 16:45.212
He packs his lunch when he leaves home
and comes back fully covered in paint.

16:45.295 --> 16:48.924
Maybe he feels embarrassed,
but he doesn't tell me where he paints.

16:49.008 --> 16:51.051
Not everyone gets to paint big pictures.

16:51.135 --> 16:53.137
-If they paint, they're painters.
-Of course. Yes.

16:53.220 --> 16:56.682
That painting is so good,
and all I want is to see his work.

17:00.102 --> 17:03.188
I've seen every one of my son's drawings
since elementary school.

17:03.272 --> 17:05.024
It's one of life's joys.

17:05.858 --> 17:08.110
I look forward to film premieres
for that reason.

17:08.193 --> 17:09.278
Hmm.

17:09.361 --> 17:13.449
Uh, our theater
would be ruined without "Park-casso."

17:20.080 --> 17:22.583
Sir, you're not from Seoul, are you?

17:28.380 --> 17:30.007
Wow!

17:39.933 --> 17:41.351
What is it this time?

17:41.435 --> 17:43.729
Did Eun-myeong sell something
at school again?

17:45.981 --> 17:47.274
Eun-myeong's mom.

17:47.858 --> 17:49.985
Don't call me that anymore, please.

17:50.069 --> 17:52.696
Should we call you
Geum-myeong's mom, then?

17:54.198 --> 17:55.532
Did I get a call from Seoul?

17:55.616 --> 17:56.825
Geum-myeong has a boyfriend.

17:56.909 --> 17:59.411
Of course she's not thinking about
Mom and Dad.

17:59.995 --> 18:01.830
It's unfair.

18:02.414 --> 18:04.917
It's as if calling us first
is a difficult burden.

18:05.417 --> 18:08.170
Well, they're only kids
while you're raising them.

18:08.670 --> 18:11.465
Once they leave the nest,
they're busier than the president.

18:11.548 --> 18:14.301
Children don't have time for parents
once they leave home.

18:15.302 --> 18:17.596
What, did you have another bad dream?

18:28.065 --> 18:31.944
Anyway, why did the school call you?
Eun-myeong last in his class?

18:32.027 --> 18:33.862
He's not last.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.781
Because Cheol-yong is in that class.

18:38.117 --> 18:39.785
It's about cigarettes.

18:40.994 --> 18:42.538
You promised you wouldn't spill it.

18:42.621 --> 18:44.957
So does that
sneaky little punk smoke, now?

18:45.040 --> 18:46.542
He doesn't smoke.

18:46.625 --> 18:47.835
He sold them.

18:48.502 --> 18:50.671
He sold some cigarettes.

18:51.755 --> 18:53.423
AUNTIES' SEAFOOD HOUSE

18:53.507 --> 18:54.842
He's something else.

18:54.925 --> 18:58.303
Well, I suppose it's better
to sell them than to smoke them.

18:58.387 --> 19:00.889
He goes to the general store,
lies to the old man

19:00.973 --> 19:02.599
about the cigarettes being for us,

19:02.683 --> 19:06.728
and he basically acts like
a cigarette delivery man.

19:06.812 --> 19:09.022
He even adds a markup on resale.

19:09.648 --> 19:13.944
Honestly, I'm more curious about what
Eun-myeong will become than Geum-myeong.

19:16.697 --> 19:18.824
Have you asked him why he does that?

19:18.907 --> 19:22.661
What do you mean why? He's a teenage boy.

19:22.744 --> 19:24.079
He thinks he knows it all.

19:24.163 --> 19:26.623
I mean, you've never asked the boy

19:26.707 --> 19:29.376
why he feels the need
to earn cash of his own?

19:29.459 --> 19:33.380
Oh, I'm not sure
why he's always out to make cash.

19:33.463 --> 19:35.757
Well, that's why you have to ask.

19:35.841 --> 19:38.927
You may have birthed him,
but you can't read his mind.

19:39.011 --> 19:42.014
You know, I noticed you never raise
your voice at Geum-myeong,

19:42.097 --> 19:44.308
yet you're only tough
on Eun-myeong, right?

19:44.391 --> 19:46.143
Geum-myeong's a tough cookie,

19:46.226 --> 19:49.521
but you're way too overly careful
with her, like Jell-O.

19:49.605 --> 19:53.150
Eun-myeong's a laid-back boy,
but you're so hard on him.

19:53.233 --> 19:56.445
Geum-myeong is a sensitive
and emotional girl like me,

19:56.945 --> 19:58.155
and Eun-myeong is…

19:59.156 --> 20:00.616
-Well--
-A pushover.

20:00.699 --> 20:02.534
-Is that it?
-Come on, I never thought that.

20:03.035 --> 20:07.206
If you keep hammering tough shells,
maybe they'll seem unaffected at first,

20:07.289 --> 20:10.626
but eventually, you will start to see
cracks on the surface.

20:11.126 --> 20:14.379
Don't show your children favoritism, ever.

20:14.922 --> 20:16.131
'Cause they will

20:16.798 --> 20:18.258
always remember.

20:18.342 --> 20:21.136
Well, it's 'cause
this is just so irritating.

20:21.803 --> 20:25.265
Oh, but I can't change
that he does things that are so awful.

20:25.349 --> 20:28.769
It's not because Geum-myeong is a child
you can gloat about

20:28.852 --> 20:31.104
and Eun-myeong is one
that you're embarrassed of?

20:32.022 --> 20:34.233
So what? I'm no saint.

20:35.192 --> 20:36.026
So what?

20:36.526 --> 20:37.527
So what?

20:40.364 --> 20:42.824
…may be the star of tomorrow.

20:43.825 --> 20:46.078
A forward-thinking choice.

20:46.161 --> 20:48.538
High-performance Elantra.

21:02.719 --> 21:03.553
So…

21:05.347 --> 21:08.267
I'm indebted to you again.
How can I repay you?

21:08.350 --> 21:09.184
Ah…

21:09.977 --> 21:11.395
Don't worry about it.

21:12.354 --> 21:14.982
See, I would love to…

21:18.610 --> 21:19.653
Mm…

21:20.570 --> 21:23.949
If you, uh…
Could you do a painting for me?

21:24.032 --> 21:26.702
That way, I might get a high price for it.

21:26.785 --> 21:29.705
Picasso's work got valuable
after he died, I heard.

21:30.622 --> 21:34.710
Is there any form of guarantee
you'll live longer?

21:36.503 --> 21:37.379
Uh…

21:40.924 --> 21:42.342
-Were you joking?
-Uh, yeah, yeah.

21:42.426 --> 21:43.260
Ah.

21:46.555 --> 21:48.974
-I'll go back to the box office now.
-Well…

21:51.226 --> 21:52.644
Yes?

21:54.062 --> 21:55.063
Thanks so much, really.

21:55.147 --> 21:57.858
No. It's not like I paid or anything.

21:57.941 --> 22:00.485
No, I mean, my mother, uh…

22:06.867 --> 22:08.994
It's her first time watching
a movie in a theater.

22:17.711 --> 22:19.713
Oh no. You have to run.

22:19.796 --> 22:22.215
No, you have to run. Have to run.

22:31.683 --> 22:34.853
She watches This Weekend's
Classic Movie on TV every week.

22:35.520 --> 22:38.732
I guess I've been too focused
on living my own life.

22:47.616 --> 22:50.869
Our loved ones
who sway our hearts.

22:50.952 --> 22:52.079
You know, son?

22:52.746 --> 22:53.997
I started crying from the moment

22:54.081 --> 22:56.166
the projectionist with glasses
walked in the room.

22:56.249 --> 22:57.084
Alfredo?

22:57.167 --> 22:58.168
Uh-huh.

22:58.251 --> 23:00.754
How come there was no fire extinguisher
in the projection room?

23:00.837 --> 23:03.298
Why did he have to put out the fire?
He should've saved himself.

23:03.382 --> 23:05.133
He should've jumped out the window.

23:05.217 --> 23:07.469
Then he would've only broken his legs.

23:08.345 --> 23:09.179
Hmm.

23:09.679 --> 23:12.516
I wonder what he did
for a living after he lost his job.

23:12.599 --> 23:15.477
Maybe Toto sent him money
because he's a nice boy.

23:15.560 --> 23:18.021
Did you cry because
Alfredo couldn't make a living anymore?

23:18.105 --> 23:20.690
You know, Toto is

23:22.025 --> 23:23.318
like you, my son.

23:26.405 --> 23:27.989
Toto reminds me of you.

23:29.908 --> 23:32.369
Ah, so, uh,
what did you wanna give to Ms. Yang?

23:32.452 --> 23:33.537
I'll give it to her.

23:35.080 --> 23:36.706
Ms. Yang, your major's English lit?

23:37.791 --> 23:39.042
Yes.

23:39.126 --> 23:40.877
PHOTOCOPY, PRINTING, BINDING

23:40.961 --> 23:44.005
You can rely on me until you graduate.

23:45.882 --> 23:49.219
These are all in English.
People just won't pick them up.

23:49.302 --> 23:51.513
The total price of these books
is quite a lot.

23:51.596 --> 23:53.473
English books are more expensive.

23:54.349 --> 23:56.101
Some of these even have notes in them.

23:56.184 --> 23:59.104
I don't know if I can accept all of these.

24:00.313 --> 24:02.732
This has to be why some prefer daughters.

24:02.816 --> 24:06.153
I'm here all day, 365 days a year.

24:06.236 --> 24:09.614
Seeing my son's work at movie premieres
is as much excitement as I can get.

24:09.698 --> 24:12.367
But today, I was absolutely happy.

24:13.160 --> 24:14.077
All thanks to you.

24:14.161 --> 24:17.038
You know, I think
I'll remember this day until I die.

24:19.958 --> 24:23.170
Uh, well,
now that you've said that,

24:23.253 --> 24:27.340
I feel like, maybe,
I did an incredible thing.

24:29.009 --> 24:30.760
Oh, Mother, stop adding to the box.

24:31.636 --> 24:33.472
How is she supposed to carry them all?

24:33.972 --> 24:36.183
She can't lift this by herself.

24:37.684 --> 24:38.643
Not by herself.

25:05.921 --> 25:07.130
Want a drink?

25:07.714 --> 25:09.466
Dri… dri… dri… dri…

25:09.966 --> 25:10.967
Drink?

25:11.051 --> 25:12.677
-No drinks, then?
-Your order.

25:12.761 --> 25:14.137
-Yeah.
-Go on. Take it.

25:14.221 --> 25:15.472
-Thank you.
-I don't think so.

25:16.014 --> 25:17.724
-Uh, so, yeah.
-Okay.

25:23.188 --> 25:24.523
So…

25:26.358 --> 25:27.400
Um, yes?

25:27.484 --> 25:31.154
If you're thankful, instead of noodles,
um, could you help me…

25:31.238 --> 25:32.155
Oh.

25:33.990 --> 25:38.495
Your girlfriend keeps knocking my shoes
out of the way at my front door.

25:40.247 --> 25:42.874
She's aware that there's nothing
going on between us.

25:43.875 --> 25:45.293
I think it's her way of

25:46.169 --> 25:48.255
processing guilt before she gets married.

25:49.464 --> 25:53.301
Oh, so you're letting
your girlfriend marry another man?

25:56.304 --> 25:59.683
Wow. How… laid-back of you.

26:00.433 --> 26:03.603
Mm. The man she's marrying
is a noodle shop owner's son.

26:03.687 --> 26:05.480
Are they rich because of noodles?

26:06.439 --> 26:07.732
Pildong Noodles.

26:12.237 --> 26:14.489
Really a perfect family to marry into.

26:15.490 --> 26:16.491
She's hesitant

26:18.076 --> 26:19.369
for some reason, but…

26:20.453 --> 26:21.955
So convince her not to marry him.

26:22.622 --> 26:25.959
If she lets go of Picasso
for the noodles guy, that's her choice.

26:26.459 --> 26:28.003
You can say to her face,

26:28.628 --> 26:31.548
"You can marry that guy if you want.
Not my loss."

26:33.425 --> 26:34.968
Or give her family a gift and say,

26:35.051 --> 26:37.387
"May I ask for
your daughter's hand in marriage?"

26:37.887 --> 26:40.432
At least try so you don't
have regrets afterwards.

26:40.515 --> 26:43.101
How would you know if I'm better than him?

26:43.685 --> 26:46.021
You don't know me… that well.

26:46.104 --> 26:47.480
Your mom loves you a lot.

26:52.444 --> 26:54.779
So that's why you paint whatever you want.

26:56.156 --> 26:59.075
You have
a deep-seated stubbornness in you.

27:01.328 --> 27:03.371
See, I'm precious to my parents too.

27:04.497 --> 27:07.876
I'd like to think that having my chin up

27:08.710 --> 27:11.004
is how I'm the pride
of my mother and father.

27:12.505 --> 27:14.424
I'd like to think that. I would.

27:18.511 --> 27:19.596
So…

27:20.680 --> 27:23.141
You don't have to take my side.
You don't even know me at all.

27:23.224 --> 27:24.517
What do you mean?

27:25.226 --> 27:27.187
You befriend folks
and realize life is life.

27:27.270 --> 27:28.396
No, we're different.

27:29.439 --> 27:31.983
If you get to know them,
there's wickedness in all people.

27:32.067 --> 27:32.901
There is.

27:36.154 --> 27:37.781
There was a time

27:37.864 --> 27:41.409
when showing kindness to strangers
was dangerous.

27:41.910 --> 27:44.996
Less than three months
after a 13-year-old was murdered

27:45.080 --> 27:46.331
in the Hwaseong serial killings…

27:46.414 --> 27:49.417
Oh my. I am so sorry again.

27:50.835 --> 27:52.754
Yes, please let me know.

27:52.837 --> 27:53.922
Please.

27:54.005 --> 27:56.049
Those bastards deserve
to be beaten to death.

27:56.132 --> 27:58.551
We have the phrase
"beat to death" for a reason.

27:58.635 --> 28:00.345
How can a man be that evil?

28:00.428 --> 28:02.681
Oh, is that right?

28:02.764 --> 28:05.767
Oh, okay.
Oh, please, please tell Geum-myeong to…

28:06.559 --> 28:09.145
to call me when she gets home
if you could…

28:10.188 --> 28:12.148
Oh, okay, okay, okay.

28:12.232 --> 28:13.191
Thanks.

28:13.817 --> 28:16.444
When you kidnap a child,
you're not taking one life.

28:16.528 --> 28:18.947
You snuff out
three of them at the same time.

28:19.030 --> 28:21.533
How can parents cope with losing a child?

28:27.664 --> 28:31.543
Losing a child is devastating for anyone,

28:31.626 --> 28:33.962
but if that's how you lose your child…

28:34.045 --> 28:34.879
Goodness.

28:37.507 --> 28:40.176
Why? Is Geum-myeong out late again?

28:40.802 --> 28:43.138
I can't figure out
what she's up to so late.

28:43.722 --> 28:45.724
I told her to stay home once the sun sets.

28:45.807 --> 28:48.101
Why? You're still having bad dreams?

28:48.852 --> 28:49.686
About what?

28:53.606 --> 28:57.110
It could relate to
the ancestral rite coming up.

28:57.694 --> 29:00.697
As a child, on that rites day,
you had something happen.

29:00.780 --> 29:02.407
You mean Aegi Hill?

29:02.490 --> 29:04.492
That hill you and I climbed together,
remember?

29:04.576 --> 29:07.746
Just thinking about it
gives me chills.

29:09.789 --> 29:11.875
I still recall the smells

29:12.500 --> 29:14.002
on the hill that day.

29:47.827 --> 29:50.914
Hurry up, now.
There's meat on the ancestral rite table.

29:50.997 --> 29:53.541
My dad will give it all to my brother.

29:53.625 --> 29:55.126
You see that black dragonfly?

29:55.210 --> 29:59.088
It's only visible to people
but not to other dragonflies.

29:59.172 --> 30:00.006
Why not?

30:00.089 --> 30:02.425
It's the Grim Reaper for dragonflies.

30:04.052 --> 30:05.595
It's the same for us.

30:06.179 --> 30:08.515
We can't see our Reaper either.

30:14.229 --> 30:16.564
What is it? Are you gonna catch it?

30:16.648 --> 30:17.899
You go ahead first.

30:18.566 --> 30:20.151
Let's just go.

30:21.069 --> 30:24.823
If I catch that one,
other dragonflies won't be killed.

30:25.323 --> 30:28.868
Baby dragonflies probably want to live
with their parents too.

30:29.786 --> 30:31.996
Ae-sun, my dad's gonna yell at you again.

30:32.956 --> 30:35.875
Was that what people call being bewitched?

30:35.959 --> 30:37.418
I don't know why I chased it.

30:59.524 --> 31:03.778
AEGI HILL
BUS STOP

31:17.750 --> 31:21.546
I need to ride the bus,
but I hurt my leg, so

31:23.047 --> 31:24.674
could you go to that store

31:25.383 --> 31:27.760
and change this coin to ten hwans?

31:41.900 --> 31:43.484
What did the shop owner say?

31:44.861 --> 31:46.154
That he's not a local bank.

31:47.322 --> 31:48.406
Did he yell at you?

31:48.907 --> 31:51.826
No, but he did give me side-eye.

31:53.703 --> 31:55.079
That is for your help.

31:59.751 --> 32:02.503
You're a very sweet girl
and kind-hearted too.

32:04.172 --> 32:06.299
Obedient as well, aren't you?

32:06.382 --> 32:09.928
But… you don't have to give me this.

32:10.011 --> 32:12.138
Well, then will you help me
get more change?

32:12.639 --> 32:15.058
Because I need to ride
two different buses.

32:20.772 --> 32:23.149
Since the store owner
didn't like giving you change,

32:24.150 --> 32:28.488
go find the cabbage truck vendor
in the alley behind the telephone pole.

32:29.781 --> 32:31.783
Could you get some change from that man?

32:32.367 --> 32:34.994
Then… I'll give you another coin.

32:37.497 --> 32:39.958
My legs hurt pretty badly, as you can see.

33:11.948 --> 33:14.367
What are you doing here?

33:14.450 --> 33:16.577
-Mom?
-What are you up to?

33:17.704 --> 33:20.373
-What are you doing here, Mom?
-Who gave you this money?

33:23.126 --> 33:24.752
-Sir!
-What?

33:24.836 --> 33:26.796
You know that guy?

33:34.512 --> 33:35.471
Huh?

33:35.972 --> 33:38.683
That lady was here just now.

33:39.726 --> 33:42.437
Gwang-rye said
her heart was pounding out of her chest,

33:42.520 --> 33:45.732
but she couldn't say anything
because she didn't want to scare you.

33:45.815 --> 33:48.151
But, Mom, what are you doing here?

33:50.069 --> 33:52.447
It was such an odd coincidence.

33:52.530 --> 33:55.742
I was in a neighborhood
that I had never gone to,

33:55.825 --> 33:59.912
and I met my mom, who would
never ever go to that neighborhood.

34:00.538 --> 34:02.498
You still don't know, do you?

34:02.582 --> 34:05.543
Your mother went out
looking for you that day.

34:12.258 --> 34:14.635
I love that I don't have to get firewood,
thanks to you.

34:14.719 --> 34:16.179
What's the big deal?

34:16.262 --> 34:18.681
We still have plenty of the wood
you brought last time.

34:19.390 --> 34:21.142
This is the least she can do.

34:21.225 --> 34:24.812
Her child's been living and eating here
for free for years.

34:24.896 --> 34:28.274
She should do that much
for her child support at least.

34:30.526 --> 34:31.903
Don't have Ae-sun carry firewood.

34:32.862 --> 34:35.323
Get rid of jeongjong
and put makgeolli on the table.

34:35.823 --> 34:37.450
That's what Han-gyu likes best.

34:39.202 --> 34:40.203
Where is Ae-sun?

34:40.286 --> 34:42.872
She doesn't care
that it's her dad's death anniversary.

34:42.955 --> 34:44.999
She just wants to roam all around town.

34:45.083 --> 34:49.003
Where's Ae-sun?
We have meat stew. Where is she?

34:50.546 --> 34:52.465
She ran after a Grim Reaper dragonfly.

34:53.257 --> 34:54.217
What?

34:55.093 --> 34:57.512
A mother's instinct
is a powerful thing.

34:58.012 --> 35:01.015
Apparently, she climbed up and down
a mountain that day.

35:05.520 --> 35:07.688
You have to eat
the meat stew for your dad.

35:08.189 --> 35:10.191
Why did you run off
instead of eating the stew?

35:17.198 --> 35:18.241
Give it to me.

35:18.825 --> 35:19.909
Why?

35:19.992 --> 35:21.744
But this one is mine.

35:21.828 --> 35:22.662
It's bad luck.

35:37.426 --> 35:39.512
How did you know I was here?

35:40.555 --> 35:42.932
I have eyes on the back of my head, dear.

35:43.015 --> 35:44.183
That's what moms need.

35:47.061 --> 35:49.522
Do you think that lady
will come to get her money?

35:52.650 --> 35:53.943
-Ae-sun.
-Hmm?

35:54.527 --> 35:55.653
Did the woman see your face?

35:56.612 --> 35:57.446
She did.

35:58.698 --> 35:59.532
Tell me.

36:00.158 --> 36:01.409
What's she look like?

36:01.492 --> 36:04.495
Well, she had a pale face

36:04.579 --> 36:06.330
and odd scratches on one wrist.

36:06.414 --> 36:08.457
Can you imagine your mother
not going after someone

36:08.541 --> 36:10.293
who'd laid a hand on her child?

36:16.507 --> 36:18.718
Come see today's first catch!

36:19.302 --> 36:21.137
Come take a look!
We'll give you a good rate.

36:21.220 --> 36:23.973
Directly from haenyeos. Three for 50 hwan.

36:24.473 --> 36:27.268
-Come on. It's a good deal.
-Fine. Give me one more. One more.

36:27.351 --> 36:30.479
It's the price
for risking our lives diving for these.

36:30.563 --> 36:32.190
Oh, forget it. I don't want it.

36:32.273 --> 36:33.107
Goodness.

36:34.192 --> 36:35.443
What are you doing?

36:38.112 --> 36:38.946
Oh, enough!

36:39.530 --> 36:42.950
Are you going to look at the wrist
of every woman in Jeju? Really?

36:47.038 --> 36:50.499
You're driving all our customers away
by yanking their wrists.

36:50.583 --> 36:53.044
Have you been here
trying to find the criminal?

36:53.127 --> 36:55.838
That cow saw my daughter's face. Her face.

36:57.548 --> 36:59.217
-I'm gonna get some conches.
-Ah.

36:59.717 --> 37:00.927
Conch is basically free.

37:01.010 --> 37:03.054
-Hurry up and eat.
-What's your price for these?

37:05.389 --> 37:06.641
Well, how much are you offering?

37:09.018 --> 37:10.978
Hey, I sent the boat away.

37:11.812 --> 37:13.773
Why are you always after young girls?

37:13.856 --> 37:16.067
Is there an age limit
on who can be a beggar?

37:18.069 --> 37:19.820
If you touch it, you gotta buy it.

37:21.906 --> 37:23.908
They get disobedient if they're too old.

37:23.991 --> 37:25.993
We need kind and sweet children.

37:27.245 --> 37:29.121
That one was exactly right.

37:30.039 --> 37:30.873
Goodness.

37:31.374 --> 37:32.458
What the hell?

37:32.541 --> 37:34.877
You can check her wrist
after we sell her something.

37:34.961 --> 37:36.837
This lady must've lost her mind.

37:36.921 --> 37:39.090
What the hell is wrong with you?
Let her go!

37:41.676 --> 37:44.136
What the hell? She's strong as a boar.

37:44.220 --> 37:48.224
You piece of shit. Were you going to have
my daughter beg for money?

37:49.016 --> 37:51.060
What? You bitch!

37:53.104 --> 37:54.188
Get them!

37:54.272 --> 37:55.398
Get those people!

37:55.940 --> 37:57.400
Get those damn infidels!

37:57.483 --> 37:58.943
Hey, get over here!

38:00.027 --> 38:01.946
My daughter? How dare you!

38:05.825 --> 38:06.993
You bitch!

38:11.080 --> 38:12.581
So what happened?

38:16.544 --> 38:19.046
So she beat her to death,
obviously.

38:19.130 --> 38:20.756
Beat her to death?

38:20.840 --> 38:24.385
She and her partner
absolutely deserved to be beaten to death.

38:25.177 --> 38:26.971
Get away, you crazy!

38:27.054 --> 38:28.472
Die, you bitch!

38:43.487 --> 38:44.613
In those days,

38:44.697 --> 38:47.241
there was no proper legal system
in this country,

38:48.075 --> 38:53.289
so the police didn't say a lot
if you killed someone who deserved it.

38:53.956 --> 38:57.043
If you take a man
who's practically dead to the station,

38:57.543 --> 38:59.462
the police would just phone it in.

38:59.962 --> 39:02.089
They actually used to
beat people to death.

39:03.883 --> 39:06.677
It happened to be
the day of his ancestral rite.

39:07.845 --> 39:11.307
Your mother said
your father saved you that day.

39:11.807 --> 39:13.017
I disagree.

39:13.100 --> 39:15.519
Your mother saved her child that day.

39:15.603 --> 39:18.105
Nothing beats a mother's instinct.

39:18.189 --> 39:20.149
Oh.

39:20.733 --> 39:22.276
Mama's up late tonight.

39:22.902 --> 39:24.278
She may forget some things,

39:24.362 --> 39:27.698
but she doesn't forget the day
we celebrate her elder son.

39:27.782 --> 39:30.951
Nothing beats a mother's instinct.

39:31.827 --> 39:34.955
My mother once said to me…

39:36.749 --> 39:38.793
"…I have eyes on the back of my head."

39:39.377 --> 39:40.961
"That's what moms need."

39:51.597 --> 39:52.431
Hey.

39:52.932 --> 39:54.058
You have a call.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.017
Okay.

39:58.687 --> 40:00.189
My goodness.

40:00.272 --> 40:03.317
Do people in Jeju not watch
Eyes of Dawn or what?

40:03.401 --> 40:05.653
She always calls when this show's on.

40:06.153 --> 40:08.364
Yeah, everything's fine.

40:10.116 --> 40:12.201
Anyway, what could happen in a day?

40:13.244 --> 40:15.162
EYES OF DAWN

40:16.414 --> 40:19.083
Are you going to call me
every time you have a dream?

40:19.166 --> 40:22.420
Why are you home so late every night?
Where are you going every evening?

40:22.503 --> 40:24.463
You're acting kind of crazy.

40:24.547 --> 40:27.716
Did they fix that street light
in that nearby alley?

40:27.800 --> 40:31.011
It's a scary world out there.
You need to be home early.

40:31.095 --> 40:32.555
Sleep at home.

40:32.638 --> 40:35.224
Never outside.
'Cause I can feel it if you do.

40:35.307 --> 40:38.102
Do you call each night
'cause you think I'll have too much fun?

40:38.185 --> 40:40.771
You're not dating anyone, are you?

40:41.647 --> 40:43.774
I won't be able to bear it
if you upset me too.

40:43.858 --> 40:46.527
You are your mom and dad's pride.

40:46.610 --> 40:49.822
My hopes are all in you, so if the pillar
of this home starts doing reckless things…

40:49.905 --> 40:51.157
That damn pillar of the home.

40:53.909 --> 40:55.578
Um, why's your hope all in me?

40:56.162 --> 40:57.913
Do you not have your own life?

40:57.997 --> 40:59.081
Think about it.

40:59.165 --> 41:02.251
Even if I sleep somewhere else,
what can you do from over there?

41:02.334 --> 41:05.504
If I wanted to fool you,
I could do it a hundred times over, Mom.

41:05.588 --> 41:06.589
Well, that's wonderful.

41:06.672 --> 41:09.383
So stop worrying about it, okay?

41:09.967 --> 41:10.968
Please.

41:11.051 --> 41:12.928
You need to live your own life.

41:13.721 --> 41:18.017
Try having a child.
Try having a child that's just like you.

41:19.810 --> 41:23.022
You wear those hairpins every day,
and I keep looking for them all the time.

41:23.522 --> 41:26.192
Why do I bother buying them for you?
You keep losing them anyway.

41:27.610 --> 41:29.945
Thinks she's better than everyone,
am I right?

41:31.697 --> 41:34.992
I got these at the hardware store,
so I just bought a set.

41:38.037 --> 41:40.080
Go visit her in Seoul
and install them yourself.

41:41.081 --> 41:44.084
I bet she can do it herself
since she's all that,

41:44.793 --> 41:46.754
and I'm the only one who's worried.

41:47.671 --> 41:50.174
Babies are only children
until they leave the nest.

41:50.257 --> 41:51.091
Jeez.

41:52.551 --> 41:54.470
She may have grown into an adult now,

41:54.553 --> 41:56.972
but I see her the same way I always have.

41:58.182 --> 41:59.808
Is this about that dream?

42:00.851 --> 42:03.896
What is this dream you keep having?

42:06.941 --> 42:10.110
Why won't you say anything?
You still having nightmares?

42:10.903 --> 42:14.114
It's not a nightmare. It's nothing much.

43:20.598 --> 43:23.684
Oh, for goodness' sake.

43:23.767 --> 43:27.396
I told you I'd give you candy
after your food was done, didn't I?

43:27.479 --> 43:29.815
Give me a hug! Mommy!

43:29.898 --> 43:31.358
Give me a hug!

43:31.942 --> 43:34.111
Miss Oh! Miss Oh!
Geum-myeong is in trouble!

43:34.194 --> 43:36.697
Is she bleeding? Tell me! Tell me!

43:53.672 --> 43:57.468
Oh! I told you I'd give you candy
after your food was done.

43:57.551 --> 43:59.219
-Mommy.
-Why don't you ever listen to Mommy?

43:59.303 --> 44:00.929
Mommy.

44:07.394 --> 44:08.437
Another nightmare?

44:14.818 --> 44:16.862
What are you dreaming about these days?

44:20.908 --> 44:23.786
I told you I'd give you candy
after your food was done.

44:23.869 --> 44:26.372
-Ms. Oh!
-Is she bleeding? Tell me! Tell me!

45:47.786 --> 45:48.620
Darling.

45:51.582 --> 45:52.624
Look, my darling.

45:54.710 --> 45:56.920
I'll get your sister,
and I'll be right back.

45:58.297 --> 45:59.131
Okay?

46:03.635 --> 46:05.095
I'll be right back.

46:11.351 --> 46:12.686
When I return,

46:13.854 --> 46:15.773
I'll give you candy every day.

46:17.065 --> 46:18.066
Hmm?

46:21.195 --> 46:22.738
Mom has suffered

46:23.947 --> 46:26.158
so many great losses.

46:33.499 --> 46:35.584
Maybe that's why she worried more.

46:36.168 --> 46:41.089
She believed that always being vigilant
could stop misfortunes from happening.

46:41.173 --> 46:43.008
Geum-myeong. Geum-myeong.

46:48.472 --> 46:49.473
Honey?

46:50.182 --> 46:51.433
Honey? Honey?

46:52.142 --> 46:53.018
Honey?

46:54.061 --> 46:55.854
Baby? Baby?

47:05.030 --> 47:06.698
Oh God. Oh no. Oh God.

47:07.741 --> 47:08.784
Oh, honey. Darling.

47:09.451 --> 47:10.619
Honey. Oh God.

47:13.747 --> 47:14.748
Help me.

47:16.583 --> 47:17.417
Help!

47:18.001 --> 47:19.837
Baby. Baby.

47:20.587 --> 47:22.130
What's wrong with you?

47:23.173 --> 47:24.091
Baby.

47:24.800 --> 47:25.968
We need

47:27.594 --> 47:28.804
to call the doctor.

47:32.266 --> 47:34.643
Somebody.

47:35.185 --> 47:37.604
Somebody, call the… the ambulance.

47:39.439 --> 47:41.900
Call for an ambulance. Okay, Gwan-sik?

47:42.651 --> 47:45.320
Why won't anyone call for the ambulance?

47:49.533 --> 47:50.784
Geum-myeong. Geum-myeong.

47:50.868 --> 47:52.202
Geum-myeong. Geum-myeong.

48:07.426 --> 48:08.343
Help!

48:09.386 --> 48:12.014
Help! Ambulance!

48:12.556 --> 48:14.308
Call an ambulance! Somebody!

48:18.520 --> 48:19.354
Baby!

48:45.255 --> 48:49.384
Hey. Why… why did you just… just
walk in here like this, huh?

48:49.468 --> 48:51.762
She's inhaled carbon monoxide.

48:51.845 --> 48:52.679
Carbon monoxide!

48:53.639 --> 48:55.349
Oh! Oh no!

48:55.432 --> 48:56.475
Bongcheon.

48:56.975 --> 48:59.645
Bongcheon 5-dong San-108.

48:59.728 --> 49:01.021
108!

49:01.730 --> 49:03.523
108! Yes!

49:04.232 --> 49:06.652
No, no, you need to climb the stairs.

49:06.735 --> 49:08.320
It's impossible to drive here.

49:08.403 --> 49:09.905
Yes, yes.

49:15.202 --> 49:18.121
In a time
when kindness was hard to find…

49:18.205 --> 49:19.623
Oh God. Oh God. Oh God. Oh God.

49:20.290 --> 49:21.249
Baby.

49:22.125 --> 49:24.252
Baby. Mom's right here. Right here.

49:25.212 --> 49:28.590
…when all three major unsolved
crime cases took place in Korea,

49:29.091 --> 49:32.886
Mom called me every night
after the nine o'clock news was over.

49:33.387 --> 49:34.930
Here! We're here! Right here!

49:35.013 --> 49:36.348
Her nerves would annoy me.

49:36.431 --> 49:37.432
Here!

49:38.183 --> 49:39.351
Here, here! Sir!

49:39.434 --> 49:43.105
But it was her nerves
that saved me that day.

49:50.570 --> 49:52.239
It's so quiet.

49:59.871 --> 50:01.331
Honey.

50:01.873 --> 50:03.583
Oh, my dear.

50:04.334 --> 50:05.585
Baby.Oh!

50:07.379 --> 50:09.631
Are you okay? Oh, goodness.

50:09.715 --> 50:13.051
Just like that,
she's saved me countless times.

50:28.942 --> 50:30.193
Oh. Oh my!

50:34.114 --> 50:35.949
Oh no. Honey! Hey, babe!

50:36.033 --> 50:37.409
Oh! Oh!

50:43.707 --> 50:46.209
You better treat your parents
well when you grow up.

50:46.293 --> 50:47.377
If you're so much trouble,

50:47.461 --> 50:50.338
I hope it's because
you're gonna accomplish big things.

50:50.422 --> 50:51.506
Will it leave a scar?

50:51.590 --> 50:53.216
You're worried about her scar?

50:53.300 --> 50:55.177
She's lucky it's not worse.

50:55.260 --> 50:59.306
Who would believe that her dad caught her
when she fell off the roof?

51:00.015 --> 51:01.516
-Mom.
-Oh.

51:01.600 --> 51:03.852
-Dad.
-Oh my.

51:05.479 --> 51:07.606
Why was she on the roof anyway?

51:07.689 --> 51:10.358
She was a magpie, she kept saying.

51:10.442 --> 51:12.319
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

51:12.402 --> 51:14.571
Mm-hmm. Oh.

51:16.073 --> 51:17.240
Oh, you got stitches.

51:17.324 --> 51:20.035
It must hurt so much.
You sweet little thing.

51:21.411 --> 51:22.996
Many moons later,

51:23.622 --> 51:26.249
when I could no longer
speak to her on the phone,

51:26.792 --> 51:29.419
I missed hearing her nervous voice.

51:30.670 --> 51:33.298
I'm so sorry. Mm?

51:34.007 --> 51:35.092
Sorry, honey.

51:35.842 --> 51:36.718
Sorry.

51:38.929 --> 51:40.347
It's okay. It's okay.

51:41.098 --> 51:43.600
Her heart sank
countless times.

51:44.226 --> 51:47.395
I wish I could've shown her
how much I appreciated her.

51:48.730 --> 51:52.025
When it's already too late,
regret catches up with us.

54:45.448 --> 54:50.287
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."
